heat-basis-v1 bundles items that show daily maximum temperatures from GHCN-Daily, NOAA NCEI: the
stations USW00003192, USW00003184, USW00023183 and USC00028499, as fetched on 2026-11-01.

NOAA's metadata page for the dataset (gov.noaa.ncdc:C00861) names no licence. It asks for these
two citations:

Menne, Matthew J., Imke Durre, Bryant Korzeniewski, Shelley McNeill, Kristy Thomas, Xungang Yin,
Steven Anthony, Ron Ray, Russell S. Vose, Byron E. Gleason, and Tamara G. Houston (2012): Global
Historical Climatology Network - Daily (GHCN-Daily), Version 3. Those four stations. NOAA National
Climatic Data Center. doi:10.7289/V5D21VHZ. Accessed 2026-11-01.

Matthew J. Menne, Imke Durre, Russell S. Vose, Byron E. Gleason, and Tamara G. Houston, 2012: An
Overview of the Global Historical Climatology Network-Daily Database. J. Atmos. Oceanic Technol.,
29, 897-910. doi:10.1175/JTECH-D-11-00103.1.

It also says: "NOAA and NCEI make no warranty, expressed or implied, regarding these data, nor does
the fact of distribution constitute such a warranty. NOAA and NCEI cannot assume liability for any
damages caused by any errors or omissions in these data."

